error: rsjs boundary: `rsjs::server_only(...)` cannot declare or read `memo(...)`

       Why:
         Opaque server-only boundaries render static SSR content and are not lowered into Client IR. A client primitive declared there would either be dropped or would never hydrate.

       Use one of:
         - Declare client primitives before the template and render their reachable uses normally.
         - Keep `rsjs::server_only(...)` and `rsjs::server_attr(...)` limited to plain server-rendered content.
         - Move browser behavior into a handler, binding, client helper, or descriptor prop that rsjs can lower.

       Tracked feature:
         server_boundary.client_primitive
